  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n-  Warmest temperatures today and Wednesday.\n\n-  Thunderstorm chances this afternoon, increasing in coverage and\n   northward extent for Wednesday, bringing gusty outflow and\n   lightning.\n\n-  Pacific Northwest trough brings gusty winds later this week and\n   cooler temperatures for the weekend.\n\nHigh pressure will maintain a warming trend across the Northern\nRockies today and tomorrow with high temperatures running roughly\n10 degrees above seasonal averages. Light southeasterly winds will\nreroute smoke from fires to the east causing localized reductions\nin air quality and minor impacts to long-range visibility.\n\nMonsoonal moisture will begin to surge northward today\nreintroducing shower and thunderstorm chances, primarily across\nsouthwest Montana and central Idaho, extending as far northward as\nthe I-90 corridor. Erratic outflow wind gusts of 30 to 40 mph \nwill be commonplace, with isolated stronger gusts in the 50 mph \nrange possible across southwest Montana and Lemhi County.\n\nDeeper moisture will encompass the region by Wednesday, expanding\nthe coverage of convective shower and storm chances. \n\nEnsemble forecast guidance maintains high confidence in an\napproaching Pacific northwest upper-level trough late this week\ninto the weekend. This transition will increase synoptic-scale\nwesterly and southwesterly winds for Thursday and Friday \nintroducing another prolonged period of elevated fire weather \nconditions. The incoming trough will also provoke a longer-term \nactive weather pattern with much cooler temperatures for this \ncoming weekend.",
